verdicts.revised_recommendation:
Adopt as proposed:
- M1/M6 gate: count licensed, valid, independent source families;
- split held-out by source family;
- estimate precision after the pilot (CI width versus number of clusters) before fixing study size;
- time boxes and a stop date;
- a predefined minimum viable study that cuts mutants per model first.
If fewer than about 3 independent held-out families are available, state in the preregistration that held-out generalisation is exploratory, rather than silently narrowing the claim.

Required:
- move held-out manifests and model files outside the NeuroSem repository and outside any directory opened in Claude Code sessions, and add a Read deny rule for that path as defence in depth;
- disable auto memory for NeuroSem sessions before splits are frozen;
- put the hashes in the embargoed stage-1 OSF registration (INTEG-09);
- run held-out evaluation only through one scripted command that appends to a hash-chained log;
- add a test that selection output is byte-identical with the held-out directory absent.
Optional: an encrypted archive whose key is held by Neel or a mentor. Acknowledge as a limitation that held-out models are public and may be known to both the author and the model.

Add to DECISIONS.md under N-01:
- arXiv is the preprint server if an IEEE journal is targeted; line up an endorser early;
- a JOSS paper would need the general-purpose core public at least 6 months before submission, with held-out and agent-study assets in a separate private repository;
- keep one citation metadata source;
- never enable Zenodo integration on a repository containing hidden assets.
